3... g6 { Black prepares to put the bishop on g7. } ( 3... Nge7 { The Cozio: the knight goes to e7 so that it cannot be pinned. } 4. O-O g6 5. c3 Bg7 6. d4 { White builds the centre while Black's pieces are passive. } ) ( 3... Be7 4. d4 exd4 5. Nxd4 Nf6 6. Nc3 O-O 7. O-O { Simple development and more space. } ) 4. d4 { Opens the centre before the bishop reaches g7. } 4... exd4 5. Nxd4 { Takes back, with a knight in the centre. } 5... Bg7 6. Be3 { Guards the knight on d4. } 6... Nf6 7. Nc3 { Develops and guards e4. } 7... O-O 8. O-O { White has more space and every piece on a good square. Plan: Qd2, f3 to guard e4, and a calm build-up. } *
